; XML's embedding: any plain tree as an element tree, the shape XML's
; reader builds and its render writes, and back again. This is a library
; of definitions, each named `xml-...`, which a host links with its own
; program and with the render (alchemy's `compile_sources`). It has two
; entry points: `xml-embed` takes a plain tree's events to the element
; tree's, and `xml-unembed`, its reverse, takes an element tree's events
; back to the plain tree's. Nothing else here is the host's to call.
;
; The embedding:
;
; - The root value is the element `document`.
; - An object is an element with the attribute `type="object"`. Each of
;   its members, in order, is a child element `member` whose attribute
;   `name` is the member's key and whose own content is the member's
;   value. Every member is a `member` element, whatever its key: a key
;   may be any string, an element's name may not, and one spelling for
;   every member keeps the reverse to one rule, so no member is an
;   element named by its key.
; - An array is an element with the attribute `type="array"`. Each of
;   its elements, in order, is a child element `item` whose own content
;   is the element's value.
; - A string is its element's one child, character data. An empty
;   string is an element with the attribute `type="string"` and no
;   child, so that an element with no `type` always holds text.
; - A string holding a character XML cannot carry, one outside XML 1.0's
;   production Char (U+0000 to U+0008, U+000B, U+000C, U+000E to U+001F,
;   U+FFFE and U+FFFF, which not even a character reference writes), is
;   its double-quoted JSON form, the text `quoted` makes, whose escapes
;   leave nothing XML cannot carry, in an element with the attributes
;   `type="string"` and `encoding="json"`.
; - A key XML cannot carry is written the same way: the member element's
;   `name` holds the key's double-quoted JSON form, and its attribute
;   `name-encoding="json"` says so.
; - A number is its character data, in an element with the attribute
;   `type="number"`: its lexeme, or the text JSON writes for it when it
;   has none, and XML Schema's `INF`, `-INF` or `NaN` for one that is not
;   finite, which JSON has no text for.
; - A boolean is `true` or `false`, in an element with the attribute
;   `type="boolean"`.
; - Null is an element with the attribute `type="null"` and no child.
;
; Every element's members are the reader's, in the reader's order, which
; the render holds a tree to: `name`; `localName`, the same name, since
; no name here has a prefix; `attributes`, an object; and `children`, an
; array. The attributes come in one order: `type` where the value has
; one, `encoding` where its text is encoded, and then, on a member,
; `name`, and `name-encoding` where the key is encoded. So `{"item": 1}`
; is written
;
;   <document type="object"><member type="number" name="item">1</member></document>
;
; `[1]` is written
;
;   <document type="array"><item type="number">1</item></document>
;
; and `{"k\u0000": "v\u0001"}`, a key and a string XML cannot carry, is
; written
;
;   <document type="object"><member type="string" encoding="json" name="&quot;k\u0000&quot;" name-encoding="json">"v\u0001"</member></document>
;
; The render writes nothing between two elements, neither white space nor
; a line break, and a text child as one run of character data, so the
; document it writes reads back as the element tree the embedding built.
;
; The reverse reads an element by its attributes and by its parent's
; `type`. The root element is the root value. Under an element of
; `type="object"` each child is a `member` element, whose `name` is the
; key of the member it holds, read with `unquoted` where its
; `name-encoding` is `json`, and under one of `type="array"` each child
; is an `item` element. Of the others, an element with no `type` holds
; one text, its string; `type="string"` holds one text or none, the
; empty string, and with `encoding="json"` one text, the string's
; double-quoted form, read with `unquoted`; `type="boolean"` holds `true`
; or `false`; `type="null"` holds nothing; and `type="number"` holds the
; number's text, which reads back as the number it spells, its lexeme
; kept: `INF`, `-INF` and `NaN` as the numbers that are not finite, and
; any other text by `number`. The attributes may come in any order, since
; XML gives them none.
;
; An element tree that is not an embedding fails with
; TARGET_VALUE_UNREPRESENTABLE, naming what was met: a root element not
; named `document`; a child of an object's element not named `member`,
; or of an array's not named `item`; a `localName` that is not the name;
; a `type` the embedding never writes; an `encoding` or a
; `name-encoding` other than `json`; an `encoding` on an element whose
; `type` is not `string`; an attribute other than those four, `name` or
; `name-encoding` on an element that is not a member, and an attribute
; given twice; a member without a `name`; text under an object's or an
; array's element; an element under a scalar's; a second child under a
; scalar's; a scalar's element without the text its type needs; a
; number's text holding a character no JSON number has; and a member the
; reader adds only for what the embedding never writes (`prefix`,
; `namespace`, `space`, `lang`). A tree that is not an element tree at
; all fails the same way, in the words the render's refusal uses. Two
; texts fail as the operator that reads them fails, with INPUT_INVALID,
; since alchemy reads no single character of a string and the reverse
; can test which characters a text holds but not their order: a number's
; text of a JSON number's characters that still spells no number (`1-2`),
; which `number` refuses, and an encoded text or name that is no
; double-quoted form, which `unquoted` refuses. Events no tree has fail
; with PROTOCOL_ORDER_ERROR, in both directions.
;
; Each direction's state is a stack with one marker per open container,
; so it grows with a document's nesting and never with its width or its
; length. The embedding keeps `:object` or `:array` for each open
; container of the plain tree, and, between a member's key and its value,
; the key on top, for the member element's `name`. Once the root value
; is written the state is `[:done]`, and nothing may follow it. The
; reverse keeps one marker for each open element, `[phase role kind]`:
; the phase says what the element has due next, as the render's markers
; do; the role is `:document`, `:item` or `:member`; and the kind is
; what the element holds, the `type` attribute's as a keyword
; (`:encoded` for a string of `encoding="json"`), or `:none` without a
; type. While the attributes are read the kind is what they have said so
; far, `[type encoding name name-encoding]`, each `:none` until its
; attribute is read, and when they end a member's key goes out and the
; kind is settled. Once the root element is read the state is `[:done]`.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; The embedding
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; The characters XML 1.0 can carry, its production Char, as code-point
; ranges: a tab, a line feed, a carriage return, and every character from
; the space on but the surrogates, U+FFFE and U+FFFF.
def xml-embed-chars [[9 10] [13 13] [32 55295] [57344 65533] [65536 1114111]]

; The top of the stack: `:none` before the root value, `:done` after it,
; `:object` or `:array` for the open container, or the key of the member
; whose value is due.
def xml-embed-top [s]
  match (count s)
    case 0 :none
    case _ (top s)

; A member element's name attributes, after the attributes before them:
; the key in `name`, or, where XML cannot carry it, its double-quoted
; form there and `name-encoding="json"`; `:none` stands for no member.
def xml-embed-name [name head]
  match name
    case :none head
    case _
      if (chars-within xml-embed-chars name)
        push (scalar name) (push (key "name") head)
        push (scalar "json")
          push (key "name-encoding")
            push (scalar (quoted name)) (push (key "name") head)

; An element's attributes, after its head's events: `type` where the
; value has one, `encoding` where its text is encoded, and then a
; member's name; `:none` stands for none.
def xml-embed-attributes [type encoding name head]
  xml-embed-name name
    match [type encoding]
      case [:none _] head
      case [_ :none] (push (scalar type) (push (key "type") head))
      case _ (push (scalar encoding) (push (key "encoding") (push (scalar type) (push (key "type") head))))

; The events that open an element: its name, its localName, its
; attributes, and the start of its children.
def xml-embed-head [element type encoding name]
  push array-start
    push (key "children")
      push object-end
        xml-embed-attributes type encoding name
          [object-start (key "name") (scalar element) (key "localName") (scalar element)
            (key "attributes") object-start]

; A scalar's whole element when it has no child: the empty string and
; null.
def xml-embed-leaf [element type name]
  push object-end
    push array-end (xml-embed-head element type :none name)

; A scalar's whole element when its one child is its text.
def xml-embed-text [element type encoding name text]
  push object-end
    push array-end
      push (scalar text) (xml-embed-head element type encoding name)

; A number's text: its lexeme, or the text JSON writes for it, and XML
; Schema's spelling of one that is not finite.
def xml-embed-number [value]
  match (number-class value)
    case :finite (scalar-text csv-options value)
    case :infinity "INF"
    case :negative-infinity "-INF"
    case :nan "NaN"

; A string's element: its text where XML can carry it, and otherwise its
; double-quoted form, typed `string` and encoded `json`; the empty
; string has no child.
def xml-embed-string [element name value]
  match value
    case "" (xml-embed-leaf element "string" name)
    case _
      if (chars-within xml-embed-chars value)
        xml-embed-text element :none :none name value
        xml-embed-text element "string" "json" name (quoted value)

; A scalar's element, typed as the embedding types it.
def xml-embed-scalar [element name value]
  match (kind value)
    case :string (xml-embed-string element name value)
    case :number (xml-embed-text element "number" :none name (xml-embed-number value))
    case :boolean (xml-embed-text element "boolean" :none name (scalar-text csv-options value))
    case :null (xml-embed-leaf element "null" name)

; A container opens: the root's element, an item's, or the element of
; the member whose key is on top, which the container's marker replaces.
def xml-embed-open [s type marker]
  match (xml-embed-top s)
    case :none (transition [marker] (xml-embed-head "document" type :none :none))
    case :array (transition (push marker s) (xml-embed-head "item" type :none :none))
    case :object (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a value where a key is due, which a tree's never do")
    case name (transition (push marker (pop s)) (xml-embed-head "member" type :none name))

; A scalar: the root's whole element, after which the tree is done; an
; item's; or the element of the member whose key is on top, which comes
; off.
def xml-embed-value [s value]
  match (xml-embed-top s)
    case :none (transition [:done] (xml-embed-scalar "document" :none value))
    case :array (transition s (xml-embed-scalar "item" :none value))
    case :object (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a value where a key is due, which a tree's never do")
    case name (transition (pop s) (xml-embed-scalar "member" name value))

; A key, held on top until its value opens the member's element.
def xml-embed-key [s name]
  match (xml-embed-top s)
    case :object (transition (push name s) [])
    case :array (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a key inside an array, which a tree's never do")
    case :none (fail :protocol-order "the events begin with an end or a key, which a tree's never do")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a key where a value is due, which a tree's never do")

; A container's element closes, its children and then itself, and its
; marker comes off; the root's is the tree's end.
def xml-embed-close [s]
  let [rest (pop s)]
    match (count rest)
      case 0 (transition [:done] [array-end object-end])
      case _ (transition rest [array-end object-end])

; A container's end, which must be the open container's.
def xml-embed-end [s marker]
  match [(xml-embed-top s) marker]
    case [:object :object] (xml-embed-close s)
    case [:array :array] (xml-embed-close s)
    case [:none _] (fail :protocol-order "the events begin with an end or a key, which a tree's never do")
    case [:object _] (fail :protocol-order "the events end an array inside an object, which a tree's never do")
    case [:array _] (fail :protocol-order "the events end an object inside an array, which a tree's never do")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events end a container after a key and before its value, which a tree's never do")

def xml-embed-event [s event]
  match event
    case object-start (xml-embed-open s "object" :object)
    case array-start (xml-embed-open s "array" :array)
    case (key name) (xml-embed-key s name)
    case (scalar value) (xml-embed-value s value)
    case object-end (xml-embed-end s :object)
    case array-end (xml-embed-end s :array)

def xml-embed-step [s event]
  match (xml-embed-top s)
    case :done (fail :protocol-order "the events hold more after the root value, which a tree's never do")
    case _ (xml-embed-event s event)

def xml-embed-finish [s]
  match (xml-embed-top s)
    case :done []
    case :none (fail :protocol-order "the events hold no value, where a tree's hold one")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events ended inside a container, which a tree's never do")

; The embedding: a plain tree's events in, the element tree's out.
def xml-embed [input]
  as-events (scan-emit [] xml-embed-step xml-embed-finish (events input))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; The reverse
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; The characters a JSON number's text may hold: `+`, `-`, `.`, the
; digits, `E` and `e`.
def xml-unembed-number-chars [[43 43] [45 46] [48 57] [69 69] [101 101]]

; The top of the stack: `:none` before the root element, `:done` after
; it, and otherwise the open element's marker.
def xml-unembed-top [s]
  match (count s)
    case 0 :none
    case _ (top s)

; The top marker replaced.
def xml-unembed-mark [marker s]
  push marker (pop s)

; A member met where an element has none of its own: one of the four out
; of its place, one the reader adds only for what an embedding never
; writes, or one no element has.
def xml-unembed-member [name]
  match name
    case "name" (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its member name is out of place, where an element's members are name, localName, attributes and children, in that order")
    case "localName" (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its member localName is out of place, where an element's members are name, localName, attributes and children, in that order")
    case "attributes" (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its member attributes is out of place, where an element's members are name, localName, attributes and children, in that order")
    case "children" (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its member children is out of place, where an element's members are name, localName, attributes and children, in that order")
    case "prefix" (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element has a prefix, which no element of an embedding has")
    case "namespace" (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element has a namespace, which no element of an embedding has")
    case "space" (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element has an xml:space, which no element of an embedding has")
    case "lang" (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element has an xml:lang, which no element of an embedding has")
    case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: it has a member that is not one of name, localName, attributes and children")

; A member's `name` or `name-encoding`, which no other element has: its
; value is read in the phase named for it.
def xml-unembed-member-attribute [s role a phase name]
  match role
    case :member (transition (xml-unembed-mark [phase role a] s) [])
    case _
      fail :unrepresentable
        string-join ""
          ["the element tree is not an embedding: an element that is not a member has a " name
            " attribute, which only a member's has"]

; An attribute's name: `type` and `encoding` on any element, and `name`
; and `name-encoding` on a member, each once. The kind holds what the
; attributes have said so far, `[type encoding name name-encoding]`.
def xml-unembed-attribute [s role a name]
  match [name a]
    case ["type" [:none e n ne]] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:type role a] s) [])
    case ["type" _] (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element has two types")
    case ["encoding" [t :none n ne]] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:encoding role a] s) [])
    case ["encoding" _] (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element has two encodings")
    case ["name" [t e :none ne]] (xml-unembed-member-attribute s role a :key name)
    case ["name" _] (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a member element has two names")
    case ["name-encoding" [t e n :none]] (xml-unembed-member-attribute s role a :key-encoding name)
    case ["name-encoding" _] (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a member element has two name-encodings")
    case _
      fail :unrepresentable
        string-join ""
          ["the element tree is not an embedding: an element has the attribute " (quoted name)
            ", where the embedding writes type, encoding and, on a member, name and name-encoding"]

; A key, in the phase that awaits one: an element's next member, or an
; attribute's name.
def xml-unembed-key [s m name]
  match m
    case [:name-key role t]
      match name
        case "name" (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:name role t] s) [])
        case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its first member is not name, where an element's members are name, localName, attributes and children")
    case [:local-key role t]
      match name
        case "localName" (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:local role t] s) [])
        case _ (xml-unembed-member name)
    case [:attributes-key role t]
      match name
        case "attributes" (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attributes-start role t] s) [])
        case _ (xml-unembed-member name)
    case [:attribute-key role a] (xml-unembed-attribute s role a name)
    case [:children-key role t]
      match name
        case "children" (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:children-start role t] s) [])
        case _ (xml-unembed-member name)
    case [:end role t] (xml-unembed-member name)
    case [:children role t] (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a key inside an array, which a tree's never do")
    case [:filled role t] (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a key inside an array, which a tree's never do")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a key where a value is due, which a tree's never do")

; An element's name that is not the one its role gives it.
def xml-unembed-misnamed [role value]
  match (kind value)
    case :string
      match role
        case :document (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: the root element is named " (quoted value) ", where an embedding's is document"]))
        case :member (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: a child of an object's element is named " (quoted value) ", where a member's is member"]))
        case :item (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: a child of an array's element is named " (quoted value) ", where an item's is item"]))
    case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its name is not a string")

; The element's name, which its role decides: `document` for the root,
; `member` under an object's element and `item` under an array's.
def xml-unembed-name [s role t value]
  match [role value]
    case [:document "document"] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:local-key role t] s) [])
    case [:member "member"] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:local-key role t] s) [])
    case [:item "item"] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:local-key role t] s) [])
    case _ (xml-unembed-misnamed role value)

; Its localName, which is the name, since no name of an embedding's has
; a prefix.
def xml-unembed-local [s role t value]
  match [role value]
    case [:document "document"] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attributes-key role t] s) [])
    case [:member "member"] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attributes-key role t] s) [])
    case [:item "item"] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attributes-key role t] s) [])
    case _
      match (kind value)
        case :string (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: an element's localName is " (quoted value) ", where it is the element's name"]))
        case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its localName is not a string")

; The `type` attribute's value, one of the six the embedding writes, kept
; as its text until the attributes end.
def xml-unembed-type [value]
  match value
    case "object" value
    case "array" value
    case "string" value
    case "number" value
    case "boolean" value
    case "null" value
    case _
      match (kind value)
        case :string (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: an element's type is " (quoted value) ", where the embedding writes object, array, string, number, boolean or null"]))
        case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element's type is not text")

; The value of `encoding` or `name-encoding`, which the embedding writes
; `json`, as `:json`; `what` names the attribute for a failure.
def xml-unembed-encoding [what value]
  match value
    case "json" :json
    case _
      match (kind value)
        case :string (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: " what " is " (quoted value) ", where the embedding writes json"]))
        case _ (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: " what " is not text"]))

; A member's `name`, its key or the key's double-quoted form, kept until
; the attributes end.
def xml-unembed-name-text [value]
  match (kind value)
    case :string value
    case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a member's name is not text")

; An element's kind, settled when its attributes end: its type's keyword,
; `:encoded` for a string of `encoding="json"`, or `:none` without a
; type. An encoding on an element of any other type is refused.
def xml-unembed-kind [t e]
  match [t e]
    case ["string" :json] :encoded
    case [:none :json] (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element has an encoding and no type, where an encoded string's element has the type string")
    case [_ :json] (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: an element of type " t " has an encoding, which only a string's element has"]))
    case ["object" _] :object
    case ["array" _] :array
    case ["string" _] :string
    case ["number" _] :number
    case ["boolean" _] :boolean
    case ["null" _] :null
    case _ :none

; The attributes' end: a member must have had its name, which goes out
; now, read with `unquoted` where its `name-encoding` is `json`, and the
; element's kind is settled.
def xml-unembed-attributes-end [s role a]
  match [role a]
    case [:member [t e :none ne]] (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a member element has no name attribute, where it holds its member's key")
    case [:member [t e n :none]] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:children-key role (xml-unembed-kind t e)] s) [(key n)])
    case [:member [t e n ne]] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:children-key role (xml-unembed-kind t e)] s) [(key (unquoted n))])
    case [_ [t e n ne]] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:children-key role (xml-unembed-kind t e)] s) [])

; A number's text, read back as the number it spells, its lexeme kept:
; XML Schema's `INF`, `-INF` and `NaN` as the numbers that are not
; finite, and any other text by `number`, once it is known to hold only
; the characters a JSON number has.
def xml-unembed-number [value]
  match value
    case "INF" (number "Infinity")
    case "-INF" (number "-Infinity")
    case "NaN" (number "NaN")
    case "" (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a number's element holds no text, where it holds the number's")
    case _
      if (chars-within xml-unembed-number-chars value)
        number value
        fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: a number's element holds " (quoted value) ", which is no number"])

; A scalar's text: its string where the element has no type or
; `type="string"`, the string its double-quoted form spells where it is
; encoded, `true` or `false` where it is a boolean, and the number it
; spells where it is a number.
def xml-unembed-scalar-text [s role t value]
  match t
    case :boolean
      match value
        case "true" (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:filled role t] s) [(scalar true)])
        case "false" (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:filled role t] s) [(scalar false)])
        case _ (fail :unrepresentable (string-join "" ["the element tree is not an embedding: a boolean's element holds " (quoted value) ", where it holds true or false"]))
    case :number (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:filled role t] s) [(scalar (xml-unembed-number value))])
    case :encoded (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:filled role t] s) [(scalar (unquoted value))])
    case _ (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:filled role t] s) [(scalar value)])

; A child that is text, which only a scalar's element holds.
def xml-unembed-text [s role t value]
  match t
    case :object (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an object's element holds text, where it holds member elements")
    case :array (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an array's element holds text, where it holds item elements")
    case :null (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a null's element holds text, where it holds nothing")
    case _
      match (kind value)
        case :string (xml-unembed-scalar-text s role t value)
        case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a child is a number, a boolean or null, where text is a string")

; A scalar, in the phase that awaits it.
def xml-unembed-scalar [s m value]
  match m
    case [:name role t] (xml-unembed-name s role t value)
    case [:local role t] (xml-unembed-local s role t value)
    case [:type role [t e n ne]]
      transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attribute-key role [(xml-unembed-type value) e n ne]] s) []
    case [:encoding role [t e n ne]]
      transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attribute-key role [t (xml-unembed-encoding "an element's encoding" value) n ne]] s) []
    case [:key role [t e n ne]]
      transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attribute-key role [t e (xml-unembed-name-text value) ne]] s) []
    case [:key-encoding role [t e n ne]]
      transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attribute-key role [t e n (xml-unembed-encoding "a member's name-encoding" value)]] s) []
    case [:children role t] (xml-unembed-text s role t value)
    case [:filled role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a scalar's element has a second child, where it holds one text")
    case [:attributes-start role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its attributes are not an object")
    case [:children-start role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its children are not an array")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a value where a key is due, which a tree's never do")

; A child element, whose role its parent's type decides.
def xml-unembed-child [s t]
  match t
    case :object (transition (push [:name-key :member :none] s) [])
    case :array (transition (push [:name-key :item :none] s) [])
    case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a scalar's element holds an element, where it holds its text")

; An attribute's value met as a container, where XML has text.
def xml-unembed-attribute-container []
  fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: an attribute's value is an object or an array, where XML has text"

; An object: the attributes, whose reading starts with none said, or a
; child element.
def xml-unembed-object [s m]
  match m
    case [:attributes-start role t] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:attribute-key role [:none :none :none :none]] s) [])
    case [:children role t] (xml-unembed-child s t)
    case [:filled role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a scalar's element has a second child, where it holds one text")
    case [:name role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its name is not a string")
    case [:local role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its localName is not a string")
    case [:type role t] (xml-unembed-attribute-container)
    case [:encoding role t] (xml-unembed-attribute-container)
    case [:key role t] (xml-unembed-attribute-container)
    case [:key-encoding role t] (xml-unembed-attribute-container)
    case [:children-start role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its children are not an array")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a value where a key is due, which a tree's never do")

; The children's start, which opens the value an object's or an array's
; element holds.
def xml-unembed-open [s role t]
  match t
    case :object (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:children role t] s) [object-start])
    case :array (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:children role t] s) [array-start])
    case _ (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:children role t] s) [])

; An array: the children, and nothing else an element has.
def xml-unembed-array [s m]
  match m
    case [:children-start role t] (xml-unembed-open s role t)
    case [:children role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: a child is an array, where XML has text or an element")
    case [:filled role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: a child is an array, where XML has text or an element")
    case [:name role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its name is not a string")
    case [:local role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its localName is not a string")
    case [:type role t] (xml-unembed-attribute-container)
    case [:encoding role t] (xml-unembed-attribute-container)
    case [:key role t] (xml-unembed-attribute-container)
    case [:key-encoding role t] (xml-unembed-attribute-container)
    case [:attributes-start role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: its attributes are not an object")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events hold a value where a key is due, which a tree's never do")

; An element's end: its marker comes off, and the root element's is the
; tree's end.
def xml-unembed-close [s]
  let [rest (pop s)]
    match (count rest)
      case 0 (transition [:done] [])
      case _ (transition rest [])

; An object's end: the attributes', or the element's.
def xml-unembed-object-end [s m]
  match m
    case [:end role t] (xml-unembed-close s)
    case [:attribute-key role a] (xml-unembed-attributes-end s role a)
    case [:name-key role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: an element is an object whose members are name, localName, attributes and children")
    case [:local-key role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: it has no localName, where an element's members are name, localName, attributes and children")
    case [:attributes-key role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: it has no attributes, where an element's members are name, localName, attributes and children")
    case [:children-key role t] (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: it has no children, where an element's members are name, localName, attributes and children")
    case [:children role t] (fail :protocol-order "the events end an object inside an array, which a tree's never do")
    case [:filled role t] (fail :protocol-order "the events end an object inside an array, which a tree's never do")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events end an object after a key and before its value, which a tree's never do")

; The children's end: the value an object's or an array's element holds
; closes, and a scalar's element with no child is the empty string or
; null, as its type says.
def xml-unembed-children-end [s role t]
  match t
    case :object (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:end role t] s) [object-end])
    case :array (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:end role t] s) [array-end])
    case :string (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:end role t] s) [(scalar "")])
    case :null (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:end role t] s) [(scalar null)])
    case :number (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a number's element holds no text, where it holds the number's")
    case :boolean (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: a boolean's element holds no text, where it holds true or false")
    case :encoded (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an encoded string's element holds no text, where it holds the string's double-quoted form")
    case _ (fail :unrepresentable "the element tree is not an embedding: an element with no type holds no text, where it holds its string, and an empty string's has the type string")

; An array's end: the children's.
def xml-unembed-array-end [s m]
  match m
    case [:children role t] (xml-unembed-children-end s role t)
    case [:filled role t] (transition (xml-unembed-mark [:end role t] s) [])
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events end an array that is not open, which a tree's never do")

; The root element opens: the tree's root value.
def xml-unembed-root [event]
  match event
    case object-start (transition [[:name-key :document :none]] [])
    case array-start (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: an element is an object whose members are name, localName, attributes and children")
    case (scalar value) (fail :unrepresentable "the tree is not an XML element: an element is an object whose members are name, localName, attributes and children")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events begin with an end or a key, which a tree's never do")

def xml-unembed-event [s m event]
  match event
    case object-start (xml-unembed-object s m)
    case array-start (xml-unembed-array s m)
    case (key name) (xml-unembed-key s m name)
    case (scalar value) (xml-unembed-scalar s m value)
    case object-end (xml-unembed-object-end s m)
    case array-end (xml-unembed-array-end s m)

def xml-unembed-step [s event]
  match (xml-unembed-top s)
    case :done (fail :protocol-order "the events hold more after the root element, which a tree's never do")
    case :none (xml-unembed-root event)
    case m (xml-unembed-event s m event)

def xml-unembed-finish [s]
  match (xml-unembed-top s)
    case :done []
    case :none (fail :protocol-order "the events hold no value, where a tree's hold one")
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the events ended inside an element, which a tree's never do")

; The reverse: an element tree's events in, the plain tree's out.
def xml-unembed [input]
  as-events (scan-emit [] xml-unembed-step xml-unembed-finish (events input))
